  "nextImplementation": {
    "formatOnlySplits": "Retain one explicit neutral direction context around all resulting siblings instead of assigning auto to each fragment or freezing the current computed RTL/LTR. The existing html_container extension demonstrates the needed model/view boundary.",
    "schemaBoundary": "Establish a direction-scope wrapper capability for ordinary editor schemas; do not assume every host installs HTMLContainerExtension or silently add an unsupported node.",
    "mappingAndPersistence": "Map text/node selections into the retained wrapper; retain child IDs and rich data; preserve one undo step, atomic schema/filter rejection, JSON/Yjs state and server/browser HTML equivalence.",
    "deliberateRemoval": "Keep intentional unwrap/removal of wrapper properties distinct from format-only scope retention.",
    "reparenting": "Moving a child to a different parent is a separate context change. A new wrapper around one child cannot reproduce its old shared scope. Do not claim this case solved by the sibling wrapper.",
